Apollo 16 Soil Mechanics                                                      
Lunar Self-Recording Penetrometer (LSRP) Page D-2                             
                                                                              
Plot of Pre-flight Penetration Calibration Tests                              
                                                                              
This handdrawn plot shows the results of pre-flight calibration tests of      
the actual vs. recorded penetration for Lunar Self-Recording                  
Penetrometer (LSRP) drum S/N 2003 on the Apollo 16 flight unit.  The          
actual penetration in centimeters is shown on the ordinate, ranging from      
0 to 90.  The recorded penetration on the drum in centimeters, from 0 to      
2.5, is on the abscissa.  The nine test points form a straight line.  A       
notation "Ratio Actual/Recorded = 31.3" appears at the top.                   
